<section><h2 id="details-upgraded-box">Enable Pack-a-Punched Mystery Box weapons</h2><ol><li id="guide-step-haus-jack" data-guide-step>When the ten lanterns have opened the upstairs box room, obtain Jack-in-the-Boxes from the box. Throw one at the metal square on the beam above the staircase by the Blitz machine. Its explosion removes the square.<GuideIllustrations :images='[{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;/images/remaining/asset-0308.webp&quot;,&quot;previewSrc&quot;:&quot;/images/remaining/preview/asset-0308.webp&quot;,&quot;alt&quot;:&quot;Metal square above the Blitz-side staircase&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;Metal square above the Blitz-side staircase&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;mmmrkennedy; game imagery Activision and the relevant game studio&quot;,&quot;width&quot;:2560,&quot;height&quot;:1440,&quot;source&quot;:&quot;https://mmmrkennedy.com/games/WW2/groesten_haus/groesten_haus_guide&quot;,&quot;assetId&quot;:&quot;asset-0308&quot;}]' /></li>
<li id="guide-step-haus-piano" data-guide-step>Drop a total of 10,000 Jolts into the piano beside the Mystery Box room. After the beam target and payment are complete, weapons obtained from the Mystery Box are upgraded. There is no normal Ubersprengen machine to walk up to here.<GuideIllustrations :images='[{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;/images/remaining/asset-0309.webp&quot;,&quot;previewSrc&quot;:&quot;/images/remaining/preview/asset-0309.webp&quot;,&quot;alt&quot;:&quot;Piano payment beside the box room&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;Piano payment beside the box room&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;mmmrkennedy; game imagery Activision and the relevant game studio&quot;,&quot;width&quot;:2560,&quot;height&quot;:1440,&quot;source&quot;:&quot;https://mmmrkennedy.com/games/WW2/groesten_haus/groesten_haus_guide&quot;,&quot;assetId&quot;:&quot;asset-0309&quot;}]' /></li></ol></section>
<section><h2 id="details-survival">Maintain a route and ammunition reserve</h2><ol><li id="guide-step-haus-survive" data-guide-step>The upstairs Combat Shotgun area funnels enemies for a team, while moving between floors gives a retreat route. Keep armour stocked and an escape clear before reloading or rolling the box. Use Jack-in-the-Boxes for revives and crowd control; the small rooms can trap a stationary solo player.</li></ol></section>
<h1 id="wiki_side_quests">Side Quests</h1><section><h2 id="details-challenges">Optional: Bloodraven Mountaineer</h2><ol><li id="guide-step-haus-challenges" data-guide-step>The referenced ordinary-map tasks are reaching wave 30 without a down, reaching wave 20 without being hit and killing the wave-50 Brenner. The no-hit task starts from the beginning, rather than any twenty clean waves later. Confirm the exact Dossier condition before attempting; Prologue wave-25 restrictions are a different challenge.</li></ol></section><section><h2 id="guide-sources">Sources and review</h2><p>Source-reviewed on 8 October 2026, using the references below and the research handoff. These instructions and puzzle calculations have software checks; they have not been verified in a complete in-game playthrough. Record symbols, sequences and completion cues from your match. Screenshot and community-chart creators are credited with each illustration.</p><ul><li><a href="https://mmmrkennedy.com/games/WW2/groesten_haus/groesten_haus_guide" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">mmmrkennedy illustrated guide ↗</a></li>
